.TH pam_oauthbearer 5 "August 2026" "crudeoauth" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH NAME
pam_oauthbearer \- PAM module for OAuth 2.0 bearer token authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auth
.I sufficient
.B pam_oauthbearer.so
[\fIoptions\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B pam_oauthbearer
module allows PAM-aware applications to authenticate users with signed JWT OAuth 2.0 access tokens.
It verifies the token against locally configured trusted JWKS data and applies issuer, audience, time, scope, authorized-party, algorithm, and username policy checks.
.PP
The JWT signing key is selected by
.BR kid .
JWKS entries that are not usable for signature verification, such as encryption keys, are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
Options that may occur multiple times can be specified repeatedly.
.TP
.B grace=\fIN\fR
Permits \fIN\fR seconds of clock skew when checking
.BR nbf ,
.B iat
and
.B exp .
The default is 3 seconds.
.TP
.B userid=\fICLAIM\fR
JWT claim from which the authentication username is extracted.
The default is
.BR preferred_username .
.TP
.B disallowed_username=\fIUSER\fR
Reject the resolved username if it matches \fIUSER\fR. Matching is case-insensitive.
The option may be repeated. For example,
.B disallowed_username=root
prevents a valid token from authenticating as the local root account.
.TP
.B iss=\fIURL\fR
Trusted Issuer claim value.
.TP
.B jwks=\fIPATH\fR
Path to a JWKS file containing trusted verification keys.
.TP
.B trusted_aud=\fISTRING\fR
Trusted Audience claim value. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.B trusted_azp=\fISTRING\fR
Trusted Authorized Party claim value. Optional and repeatable.
.TP
.B required_scope=\fISCOPE\fR
Require an OAuth scope. Optional and repeatable. The token's
.B scope
claim is interpreted as a space-separated scope list.
.TP
.B allowed_alg=\fIALGORITHM\fR
Optional JWT signature-algorithm allow-list. The option may be repeated.
If omitted, the built-in algorithm policy is used.
Supported names are
.BR RS256 ,
.BR RS384 ,
.BR RS512 ,
.BR PS256 ,
.BR PS384 ,
.BR PS512 ,
.BR ES256 ,
.BR ES384
and
.BR EdDSA .
.TP
.B disallowed_alg=\fIALGORITHM\fR
Optional JWT signature-algorithm deny-list. The option may be repeated.
A denied algorithm is rejected even when it is otherwise allowed.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Bearer tokens are credentials and must be protected from disclosure.
The service transporting them should provide adequate transport security.
.PP
The module only trusts signing keys from the configured JWKS data.
A JWK's key type and metadata must be compatible with the JWT signature algorithm.
Encryption-only keys, including keys marked for
.BR RSA-OAEP ,
are not used for signature verification.
.PP
The configured issuer and audience are checked, and optional authorized-party and scope restrictions can further narrow which access tokens are accepted.
The username deny-list can be used to protect privileged local account names.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
auth sufficient pam_oauthbearer.so grace=3 userid=preferred_username \\
    iss=https://sso.example.org/realms/master \\
    jwks=/usr/share/oidc/authkeys.jwks \\
    trusted_aud=ldaps://example.org/ \\
    trusted_azp=https://client.example.org/oidc/ \\
    required_scope=openid \\
    allowed_alg=RS256 disallowed_username=root
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/\fIMULTIARCH\fR/security/pam_oauthbearer.so
Typical module location on Debian multiarch systems.
.SH RETURN VALUES
.TP
.B PAM_SUCCESS
Authentication succeeded.
.TP
.B PAM_AUTH_ERR
Authentication failed or the token was rejected.
.TP
.B PAM_CRED_ERR
The configured user ID could not be extracted from the token.
.TP
.B PAM_SYSTEM_ERR
Internal module or configuration error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam (7),
.BR pam.d (5),
.BR sasl_oauthbearer (5),
RFC 7517,
RFC 8725,
RFC 9068
